Segment slider handles (start/end) could only be dragged once. Subsequent drag attempts had no effect because the gesture handlers never updated with new position values.

## Root Cause

`pointerInput(Unit)` creates gesture handlers once with captured closure values. When `startTime`, `endTime`, or `duration` change after the first drag, subsequent drags still reference the original values.

```kotlin
// Before: Handler never recreates, captures stale values
.pointerInput(Unit) {
    detectDragGestures(
        onDrag = { change, dragAmount ->
            val dragDelta = (dragAmount.x / maxWidthPx) * duration  // stale 'duration'
            val newEnd = (endTime + dragDelta).coerceIn(...)        // stale 'endTime'
            onEndTimeChanged(newEnd)
        }
    )
}

// After: Handler recreates when dependencies change
.pointerInput(duration, startTime, endTime) {
    detectDragGestures(
        onDrag = { change, dragAmount ->
            val dragDelta = (dragAmount.x / maxWidthPx) * duration  // fresh 'duration'
            val newEnd = (endTime + dragDelta).coerceIn(...)        // fresh 'endTime'
            onEndTimeChanged(newEnd)
        }
    )
}
```

## Changes

- Updated `pointerInput()` keys in `SegmentEditorDialog.kt` for both start and end handles to include `duration, startTime, endTime`
- Ensures gesture handlers recreate with current values when any dependency changes

